## Code Examples & Patterns

### CSS/Styling Layouts
```css
/* Custom CSS / CSS Modules Pattern */
.container {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 1rem; /* Generous mobile padding */
  margin-left: auto;
  margin-right: auto;
}

/* Base styles are mobile. Layer desktop above 768px */
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .container {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding: 2rem;
  }
}
@media (min-width: 1024px) {
  .container {
    max-width: 960px;
  }
}
```

### React Conditional Rendering (Hook Pattern)
```tsx
// Use ONLY when the UI architecture changes completely
import { useMediaQuery } from '../hooks/useMediaQuery';

export const Navigation = () => {
  const isDesktop = useMediaQuery('(min-width: 1024px)');

  return (
    <nav>
      {isDesktop ? <DesktopMenu /> : <MobileHamburgerMenu />}
    </nav>
  );
};
```

---

## Code Review Checklist for Cursor
When evaluating or writing code, flag the following violations:
1. [ ] Using `max-width` media queries as the primary layout strategy (should be `min-width`).
2. [ ] Fixed pixel widths on wrapper elements instead of percentage/flex/grid scaling.
3. [ ] Clickable elements smaller than 44px without explicit padding or dimensions.
4. [ ] Font sizes smaller than 16px (`1rem`) for form inputs, which triggers auto-zoom on iOS browsers.
